.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-graph 1  "graph " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-graph \- Print the import graph as text, Graphviz, Mermaid or JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx graph\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-reporter\fR] [\fB\-\-cycles\fR] [\fB\-\-focus\fR] [\fB\-\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-hyperlinks\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the import graph as text, Graphviz, Mermaid or JSON
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
text, dot, mermaid or json. Defaults to text unless a `\-\-reporter` is given
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: One line per edge, grouped by importer
.IP \(bu 2
dot: Graphviz, for `dot \-Tsvg`
.IP \(bu 2
mermaid: A fenced block that GitHub and most wikis render inline
.IP \(bu 2
json: Nodes and edges as JSON
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-reporter\fR \fI<NAME[=PATH]>\fR
Output destination: `<name>` for stdout, `<name>=<path>` for a file; repeatable. The names are the formats, and `terminal` is `text`
.TP
\fB\-\-cycles\fR
Only the edges that close a cycle
.TP
\fB\-\-focus\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Only the files this file reaches and the files that reach it
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fI<DEPTH>\fR [default: 2]
Distance from `\-\-focus` to follow
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
relaxed, standard, strict or pristine
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads. Defaults to the machine\*(Aqs parallelism
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from this file, layered over any `rqx.yaml` found
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Do not open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Keeps the session from capturing the mouse wheel for its command menu, so the terminal keeps the mouse throughout. Without it the session captures the wheel only while the menu is open
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
How a scan reports progress on stderr; `plain` prints a line every two seconds for a job log
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A bar on a terminal, nothing in CI or when stderr is redirected
.IP \(bu 2
bar: A bar whenever stderr is a terminal, CI included
.IP \(bu 2
plain: A line on stderr every two seconds and at each phase, for a job log
.IP \(bu 2
none: Nothing
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase output: `\-v` adds the configuration, the cache and every skipped file to the report; `\-vv` also prints stage timings and git commands on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-hyperlinks\fR \fI<HYPERLINKS>\fR [default: auto]
Render `file:line` in the report as a hyperlink that opens in an editor; `auto` enables it on terminals known to support hyperlinks
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal known to support them
.IP \(bu 2
always: Whenever the report is coloured
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print a report taller than the terminal directly instead of through the pager: `$RQX_PAGER`, then `$PAGER`, then `less \-FRX`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  rqx graph \-\-cycles                  only the edges that close a cycle
  rqx graph \-\-format mermaid          Mermaid output for documentation
  rqx graph \-\-focus src/api.ts        files it reaches and files that reach it
